          "message": {
            "text": "SQL query is built with an f-string interpolating the untrusted `name` argument, allowing SQL injection in find_user_by_name. Use a parameterized query instead: conn.execute(\"SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE name = ?\", (name,))."
          },
          "ruleId": "sql-injection"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/db.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 35,
                  "startLine": 33
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL query in find_users_by_domain is built with an f-string interpolating the untrusted `domain` argument into a LIKE clause, allowing SQL injection. Bind the pattern as a parameter: conn.execute(\"... WHERE email LIKE ?\", (f\"%{domain}\",))."
          },
          "ruleId": "sql-injection"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/db.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 25,
                  "startLine": 24
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "find_user_by_name catches broad Exception and returns None with no logging or re-raise, so DB/connection errors are indistinguishable from \"user not found\". Catch the specific error (e.g. sqlite3.Error) and log it, or let it propagate."
          },
          "ruleId": "bare-except"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/importer.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 22,
                  "startLine": 21
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "import_legacy_csv silently swallows all per-row exceptions with `except Exception: pass`, hiding malformed/corrupt input and producing silently incomplete results. Narrow the exception type and log skipped lines."
          },
          "ruleId": "bare-except"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/importer.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 9,
                  "startLine": 7
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "import_archive deserializes an arbitrary file with pickle.loads(). Pickle executes attacker-controlled __reduce__ code during load, so untrusted archives give remote code execution. Use json (or a schema-validated format) instead."
          },
          "ruleId": "unsafe-deserialization"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/legacy_utils.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 10,
                  "startLine": 8
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "load_session unpickles file contents with pickle.loads(). Any session file from an untrusted source allows arbitrary code execution on load. Replace with a safe format (e.g. json) or verify integrity/authenticity before deserializing."
          },
          "ruleId": "unsafe-deserialization"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/legacy_utils.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 16,
                  "startLine": 13
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "load_legacy_cache reads cache files with pickle.loads(), which is unsafe deserialization of potentially attacker-controlled cache data and can lead to arbitrary code execution. Use a safe serialization format such as json."
          },
          "ruleId": "unsafe-deserialization"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/legacy_utils.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 33,
                  "startLine": 32
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "migrate_session wraps session.pop(\"legacy_field\") in a broad `except Exception: pass`, hiding real errors. Either narrow it (e.g. KeyError) or use session.pop(\"legacy_field\", None) with no try/except."
          },
          "ruleId": "bare-except"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/main.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 13,
                  "startLine": 11
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "main() swallows every exception from db.initialize() with `except Exception: pass` and still returns 0, so a failed schema init reports success. Log/propagate the error and return a non-zero exit code."
          },
          "ruleId": "bare-except"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
